From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:01:15 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/22] lanes: a shared round's copy windows split its copy
 budget over its copying streams

Replaces the fixed three-copy start. Each shared round recomputes the copy rows it may verify (the measured shared width less each stream's pending row, else one window's max_copy) and splits them over the round's copying streams in proportion to each stream's decayed copied-row landing rate, none past max_copy, the rest by largest remainder. Two chats split 15 copies 8/7, four 4/4/4/3; a chat whose copies miss shrinks and drifts back toward the prior while it copies nothing. Lone rounds keep their width rule; priced proposers and allocate_shared_drafts rows are untouched.
